text Work must have tired Nagisa out today. I can hear her sleeping just moments after turning the lights out.
text Unable to sleep, I stare at the ceiling alone.
text @[Tomoya]
text ...
text All of the excitement I felt just moments earlier has disappeared.
text @[Tomoya]
text (My life is so satisfying right now... What am I worried about...?)
text But... I know what it is.
music BGM01.mp3
text The sight I saw with the old man.
text The view that greeted me when I turned that corner.
text As I saw it, I felt this strange, irresistable force for a moment, and I stopped in my tracks.
text As I did, the old landscape transformed into nothing but a memory...
text The no trespassing sign...
text The empty, overgrown, grassy lot on the other side...
text The path full of ditches that seemed like they could puncture a bike tire...
text My days as a child hopping my front wheel over them... All of it...
text I knew that it was never coming back.
text Even my own job is to change what the town looks like...
text Yoshino-san once told me, "That's what it means to be alive."
text Is it really impossible to live a life without change?
text And if everything around me changes...
